{"id": "EUVD-2026-108930", "enisaUuid": "6c3a24a4-6310-30bd-a4e6-8399f056e8cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: adau1372: allow sleepy powerdown GPIOs\n\ngpiod_set_value() emits a WARN when the GPIO provider indicates that it\ncan sleep, as is typical for I2C controlled GPIO expanders. Since the\npowerdown GPIO is only manipulated in process context, use the _cansleep\nvariant instead. This lets the driver use sleepy GPIOs to power off the\nchip.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58905982b0d912021325f5de84facae86cc0f2f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6cf4c3c9b7a4df0fe4cc67481b7b251cff781b29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47c0c7a051b70d396774d5dc27b23283c28c3555", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65cd0e21746b812d311e9fac6d473dd62f0ad52a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64dd172bbffe6135d79a06ddad53dd2da4d8bd62"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98956"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "098fef3c-be27-3154-8046-d4f70204b723", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "0cb225c5-00b2-32db-8005-ba01d8522f55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "13bdbf9c-ad2c-303c-8a77-4712dc3ed578", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "2891bee2-0c3a-30b1-9605-969193ab1a4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "59081882-8670-3722-8ca9-53c36e68ec3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6cd4c6459e47402ab90802eca61a18b231434053 <58905982b0d912021325f5de84facae86cc0f2f2"}, {"id": "5d7f6ef6-782c-3253-8d01-e4540f093e71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6cd4c6459e47402